post_remove() {
  cat <<'MSG'

omarchy-typewriter is removed, but some things it used outlive the package.
These may still be present:

  /etc/omarchy-typewriter/config
      a pacman backup file. If you edited it, pacman keeps it as
      /etc/omarchy-typewriter/config.pacsave rather than deleting your changes

  /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service.d/omarchy-typewriter-igpu.conf
      forces OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE=1 on ollama.service

  ~/.config/hypr/bindings.lua
      a "-- BEGIN omarchy-typewriter" block, now binding a missing command

  ~/.config/omarchy-typewriter/
      settings and, if you configured Cloudflare, an API token

  ~/.local/state/omarchy-typewriter/
      the run history behind `omarchy-typewriter stats`. Counts and timings
      only, never the text you refined

  the local model, if you pulled one:  ollama rm granite4:micro-h

MSG
}
